eps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** An operating system manages processes, memory, storage, I/O devices and protection while providing services to applications.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Operating System concepts; Functions of OS; Services of OS; System call. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Operating System problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Process is covered under “Process Management”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Process States, Process Control Block, Threads, User Level and Kernel level thread, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Process States; Process Control Block; Threads; User Level and Kernel level thread. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Operating System problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Linux installation is covered under “Linux”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Introduction to Linux, Editing files with vi, vim, gcc, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Introduction to Linux; Editing files with vi; vim; gcc. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Operating System problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

