-- Software Engineering | ESE | medium | TestId 4400093534020129 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4400093534020129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Software Engineering requires the behaviour described by software is developed through disciplined, repeatable processes that manage requirements, design, implementation and quality. Explain how Software engineering applies, outline the main steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Software Engineering requires the behaviour described by the syllabus area concerned with Metrics: The Management Spectrum 4P’s (People. Explain how Metrics: The Management Spectrum 4P’s (People applies, outline the main steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Software Engineering requires the behaviour described by the syllabus area concerned with Software Scope. Explain how Software Scope applies, outline the main steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Software Engineering requires the behaviour described by the syllabus area concerned with Reactive versus Proactive Risk Strategies. Explain how Reactive versus Proactive Risk Strategies applies, outline the main steps and justify the result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Software engineering applies systematic methods to software requirements, design, implementation, testing, deployment and maintenance, balancing quality, cost and time.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Dual role of software; Various Myths Associated with Software; Different Software Process Models; The Linear Sequential Model. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Software Engineering problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Metrics: The Management Spectrum 4P’s (People is covered under “Project Management Concepts, Requirement Engineering &”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Project, Product and Process), The W5HH Principle, Basic concept of Requirement (Functional & Non Functional), give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Project; Product and Process); The W5HH Principle; Basic concept of Requirement (Functional & Non Functional). State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Software Engineering problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Software Scope is covered under “Project Planning Scheduling & Tracking”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Feasibility Analysis, Empirical Estimation Models, Gantt Charts and Tools used, Project Planning Scheduling & Tracking, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Feasibility Analysis; Empirical Estimation Models; Gantt Charts and Tools used; Project Planning Scheduling & Tracking. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Software Engineering problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Reactive versus Proactive Risk Strategies is covered under “Risk Analysis And Management”. An appropriate explanation should define its role, describe its main components or steps, connect it to Risk Management Process, Risk Identification, Risk Projection, Risk Refinement, give a practical example, and state one limitation or verification check.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to related syllabus points such as Risk Management Process; Risk Identification; Risk Projection; Risk Refinement. State relevant assumptions, rules, components or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Software Engineering problem. Identify the objective, explain the procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention a limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

